# Verify any freshly-fetched copy against this hash before applying this
# patch to it -- if it doesn't match, the upstream file has changed (or the
# fetch is corrupt) and this patch's hunks are not guaranteed to apply
# cleanly or correctly; stop and re-check rather than force-applying.
#
# License note: find_circ itself is GPLv3 (see its own LICENSE file) -- this
# repository is MIT. This patch is kept as a diff against the upstream file,
# never as a vendored copy of find_circ.py itself, specifically to avoid
# redistributing GPLv3 source inside an MIT repository. A build that needs
# find_circ fetches the upstream file at build time, verifies its sha256
# against the value above, and applies this patch to it -- see
# containers/build_notes.md for how this is wired into an actual build.
#
# What this patch does: upstream find_circ.py (2017) targets Python 2 and
# an old pysam API. Running it under Python 3 with a current pysam fails
# in multiple places; this patch is the minimal set of changes needed to
# get it running under the server's Python 3.7.12 + pysam 0.21.0, not a
# rewrite or a style cleanup:
#   - `file(...)` -> `open(...)` (file() was removed in Python 3)
#   - integer division `/` -> `//` where an index was expected (Python 3's
#     `/` always returns float)
#   - `.decode('string_escape')` removed (that codec doesn't exist in
#     Python 3; the value is used as-is)
#   - pysam API renames: `pysam.Samfile` -> `pysam.AlignmentFile`,
#     `.pos`/`.aend`/`.tid`/`.qname` -> `.reference_start`/`.reference_end`/
#     `.reference_id`/`.query_name`, `.getrname()` -> `.get_reference_name()`
#     (all renamed in a pysam API version well past what was current in 2017)
#   - `complement()`: strips stray `\n`/`\r` before translating, and falls
#     back to "N" for any character not in the COMPLEMENT table instead of
#     raising KeyError (the original crashed on any ambiguity-code base
#     sequence reads sometimes contain)
#   - `mismatches()`: replaced a `numpy.fromstring(..., dtype=byte)`-based
#     comparison (the `fromstring` ctor used this way is deprecated/removed
#     in modern numpy) with a plain Python `sum(x != y for x, y in zip(a,b))`,
#     also handling unequal-length inputs instead of letting the original
#     silently rely on numpy's elementwise broadcast
#   - module-level `import numpy as _np` added (the inner function that
#     referenced `_np` in the original relied on an import that was only
#     ever added inside a different, unrelated function's scope)
#
# Not touched: this patch does not change find_circ's detection algorithm,
# its CLI, or its output format/columns -- only what was necessary to make
# it import and run at all under Python 3. The triplicated
# `if A is None or B is None: break` block this diff shows (three identical
# lines in a row) is preserved exactly as it exists in the server's actual
# patched copy -- it is redundant but harmless (idempotent check), and this
# patch intentionally captures what is ACTUALLY running, not a cleaned-up
# version of it; CLAUDE.md's existing description of "three bugs fixed"
# undercounts what's in this diff, which also includes the full pysam
# API-rename set above -- this patch file is now the authoritative record,
# superseding that summary.
